It controls LG Wi-Fi soundbars on the local network of the user over the
protocol of the LG Sound Bar / Wi-Fi Speaker app. This integration is not
affiliated with nor endorsed by LG Electronics; LG is a trademark of LG
Electronics.

The protocol (framing, AES-256-CBC key and IV, messages and fields) was
rewritten from python-temescal (https://github.com/google/python-temescal,
Copyright 2018 Google LLC, Apache License 2.0; version 0.5 published on PyPI
from https://github.com/mjg59/python-temescal). No code is copied: the
JavaScript implementation in src/temescal/ is a rewrite, and the names of the
inputs and sound modes come from the tables of that library and of two pull
requests of mjg59/python-temescal (#2, #3).

What real soundbars report was taken from the Home Assistant "lg_soundbar"
integration and its issues (https://github.com/home-assistant/core, Apache
License 2.0), from the captures published by albaintor/integration-lgsoundbar
(MPL-2.0, data only) and from lgsb2mqtt (https://github.com/hobbyquaker/lgsb2mqtt,
MIT License: speaker levels as an offset from their minimum, Chromecast
discovery, plain JSON answers). No code is taken from them.
